representation of critical bond percolation on the square lattice. We consider
submatching events, which prescribe how these interfaces pair finitely many
consecutive boundary points. Romik's rationality conjectures predict that the
probabilities of these events on the semi-infinite cylinder are given by
specific rational functions, which even become dyadic rationals in the
half-plane limit.
