formalism, which express these probabilities as ratios of enumeration numbers
for totally symmetric self-complementary plane partitions (TSSCPPs). These
plane partitions admit a dimer representation, allowing us to apply Kasteleyn
theory. We evaluate the resulting hypergeometric sum using Zeilberger's and
Gosper's algorithms and then take the half-plane limit $N\to\infty$. Along the
way, we derive a somewhat simplified expression for the inverse Kasteleyn
matrix entries (encoding correlations in TSSCPPs) of Ayyer and Chhita, which
might be of independent interest.
