Title: Super quantum groups of divided powers \`a la Lusztig
Authors: Iv\'an Angiono and Cristian Vay
Categories: math.QA math.RT
MSC-class: 16T05, 16T20, 17B37, 17B20, 17B22
\\
  We construct super analogues of the quantum groups of divided powers
introduced by Lusztig. We call them super analogues because the Lie-theoretical
data governing their structure is comparable to that of contragredient Lie
superalgebras. Indeed, we show that they admit PBW-type bases parametrized by
root systems of super type, and that they also have Lusztig isomorphisms giving
a representation of the corresponding Weyl groupoids. Moreover, we prove that
our super objects are equipped with a Frobenius-type morphism whose kernel is
the Drinfeld double of a finite-dimensional Nichols algebra of super type, a
super analogue of Lusztig's small quantum group, and whose cokernel is the
enveloping algebra of the semisimple Lie algebra determined by the Cartan roots
of the Nichols algebra. We carry out our construction within the framework of
Nichols algebras of diagonal type, specifically, those whose braiding is
obtained by specializing at a root of unity. This allows us to consider a
divided power integral form inside a large quantum group of De
Concini--Kac--Procesi type and then, via specialization, obtain our desired
object.
